WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:33.513
Quite a bit of snow falling up on those mountains still

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:38.985
I think until 1600 meters or so, still snow

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:41.988
that’s around 4500ft.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.623
Yeah, it's a cold week.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:47.393
I think it's going to rain almost every day.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.396
So I'll be working inside, mostly.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.934
I'm on my own. Ela is still away for her own projects

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.769
I'm going to be pointing in the wall,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.672
which is slow work on my own,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.975
and maybe also do some, electricity already

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.978
And pull some lines and connect
some lights.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.681
Yeah.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:12.151
And I have to finish the outside work
that I did the last two weeks.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.154
But with the rain, it's
better to wait a bit because

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.691
If I get a heavy trailer of gravel.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.661
It's going to sink away in the mud I think

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.462
but we'll see.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.221
water for better bonding

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:16.282
Picked up new solar panels.

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:19.151
These ones are going to be replaced.

00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:21.287
They're about 15 years old, I think.

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:22.922
So they're...

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:24.457
it's going to be quite an upgrade.

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:29.195
Those are 230W and these are 455.

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.030
And they're also bifacial.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.033
So they can charge
from the backside as well.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:40.673
And that will be beneficial on the the ones that are on the back standing up.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.608
When there’s snow in winter.

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:46.512
That will reflect some light onto it
or give some extra charge.

00:10:47.046 --> 00:10:50.049
But mostly the front is already
just a big upgrade.

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:55.588
They are slightly larger, in dimensions,

00:10:55.588 --> 00:10:58.591
so I have to rebuild the stands

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:01.827
and also just space them out slightly

00:11:01.827 --> 00:11:04.930
and a little bit higher for winter.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.933
So it's easier with clearing snow.

00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:42.421
I’ve already been rewiring a few panels.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.325
I'm connecting all of the panels

00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:49.328
to these PV combiner boxes.

00:18:50.729 --> 00:18:54.967
which kind of minimizes the, the amount of MC4 connectors

00:18:54.967 --> 00:19:01.306
because I was using those MC4 branches
to connect everything together,

00:19:01.306 --> 00:19:04.309
but at some point
they started to melt and deformed.

00:19:06.211 --> 00:19:07.579
it could be some dirt

00:19:07.579 --> 00:19:10.616
or a bad crimp, some resistance that they get too hot.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.551
So this is better.

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:17.789
Some breakers built in as well, some protection. So,

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.726
there’s going to be another one,

00:19:20.726 --> 00:19:23.729
but most of the work
will be just rebuilding the stands

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.498
because the panels are slightly bigger, so

00:19:26.498 --> 00:19:29.501
it needs to be rebuilt.

00:19:29.635 --> 00:19:34.773
So I'll show the whole overview of the installation
once we're finished.

00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:38.177
in two weeks.

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:27.446
The bumblebee is confused,

00:22:28.814 --> 00:22:32.551
They're always digging holes in between the stones.

00:22:32.584 --> 00:22:35.253
They do that on the outside here,

00:22:35.253 --> 00:22:38.623
where it's easier
because it's a soil, like a clay mortar

00:22:38.623 --> 00:22:41.626
But now that the walls are pointed,

00:22:42.761 --> 00:22:45.230
you can get it in anymore.

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:48.233
So it's interesting to see.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:52.604
Yeah, I made a good leap with the pointing of the walls,but it's it's dirty work.

00:22:52.704 --> 00:22:55.207
My hands are incredibly dry.

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:59.444
Although I wear gloves all the time,

00:22:59.678 --> 00:23:02.581
but, I think two more days, one more day pointing,

00:23:02.581 --> 00:23:06.418
so a bit of this side wall
and then the front half,

00:23:07.452 --> 00:23:09.121
and then that's done.

00:23:09.121 --> 00:23:12.324
I remember from the first cabin that it was a big job 

00:23:12.324 --> 00:23:15.327
takes a few weeks.

00:23:17.028 --> 00:23:17.829
But yeah.

00:23:17.829 --> 00:23:18.964
Almost there.

00:23:18.964 --> 00:23:23.034
And then, then the floor work,
then cleaning up outside,

00:23:23.034 --> 00:23:26.171
doing some more soil
work, filling the trenches.

00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:27.239
They're still open.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.943
But I'm waiting for some drier days
as well.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.312
May is always very rainy here

00:23:34.312 --> 00:23:37.315
as well as this week,

00:23:37.349 --> 00:23:39.217
but quite beautiful.

00:23:39.217 --> 00:23:42.220
Dramatic skies of clouds coming in.

00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:45.257
Yeah.

00:23:45.257 --> 00:23:48.260
My brother's
visiting next week with a friend

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:50.362
Ela will be back.

00:23:50.362 --> 00:23:54.366
So I think we'll do a lot of work next week

00:23:54.366 --> 00:23:55.267
Well, the week after probably

00:23:55.267 --> 00:23:58.270
Probably
because we take some days off as well.

00:24:01.173 --> 00:24:01.740
Yeah.

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:04.743
Some problems at the chicken coop...

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:07.479
The fox is there.

00:24:07.479 --> 00:24:10.916
I mean,
I have shots of him in the night, and,

00:24:12.784 --> 00:24:15.787
he's trying to get in and you can see it.

00:24:16.555 --> 00:24:19.291
Because there's more digging underneath
the chicken coop.

00:24:19.291 --> 00:24:22.260
He's trying to dig a hole underneath.

00:24:23.462 --> 00:24:25.964
But he won't be able to
because the chicken wire is going

00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:30.435
all underneath the soil,
so there's no way to come through.

00:24:31.903 --> 00:24:34.406
But he's persistent.

00:24:34.406 --> 00:24:37.409
There wasn't an attack, actually,
this week.

00:24:37.742 --> 00:24:39.211
I didn't film it because...

00:24:39.211 --> 00:24:40.712
Well, it happened very fast.

00:24:40.712 --> 00:24:43.715
It's not on camera,
but I was having lunch inside.

00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:49.488
I heard the chickens making noise.

00:24:49.621 --> 00:24:51.923
So I ran up very quickly.

00:24:51.923 --> 00:24:56.127
And then I saw the fox disappearing
in the forest with the brown chicken.

00:24:57.295 --> 00:25:03.001
But he let it go eventually,
and she was looking quite ruffled up.

00:25:03.001 --> 00:25:05.437
I think she lost a bit of her comb

00:25:05.437 --> 00:25:08.440
the red bit in the middle.

00:25:09.674 --> 00:25:11.409
But she's all right.

00:25:11.409 --> 00:25:12.410
But the fox is there.

00:25:12.410 --> 00:25:16.381
So even now, in broad daylight,
he is, trying to get in.

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:19.417
And during the day,

00:25:19.417 --> 00:25:22.921
I often let them out in the outside run,
which is not protected.

00:25:22.921 --> 00:25:25.156
Like the fox can just jump over the fence.

00:25:26.458 --> 00:25:29.461
So, yeah, that's,

00:25:29.594 --> 00:25:30.128
That's something

00:25:30.128 --> 00:25:35.867
The first year, it was just, they were out every day roaming about.

00:25:35.867 --> 00:25:38.870
And there was never a predator,
never an issue.

00:25:38.904 --> 00:25:42.807
Only with, some domestic dogs
that were off leash.

00:25:43.074 --> 00:25:46.077
That gave some problems in the weekends.

00:25:46.344 --> 00:25:49.347
But, yeah, maybe an electric fence

00:25:49.681 --> 00:25:52.651
could fix this problem.

00:25:54.619 --> 00:25:55.921
I'm keeping them inside now.

00:25:55.921 --> 00:25:58.924
And just a few times
a day, I'm just staying there,

00:25:59.791 --> 00:26:03.228
letting them outside, and,
But I have to stay there

00:26:03.328 --> 00:26:06.331
because otherwise the foxes
probably couldn't get them.

00:26:07.165 --> 00:26:09.334
So. Yeah,

00:26:09.334 --> 00:26:10.135
that’s a new thing.

